<title>USA: NY business loans fell $56 mln in Dec 25 week.</title>
<headline>NY business loans fell $56 mln in Dec 25 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $56 million to $43,492 million in the week ended December 25, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $63 million to $43,730 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally fell $1.528 billion to $782,198 million.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
